       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n**Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is 5 times the usual maximum.** The usual adult dose is 2.5\u201310 mg once daily, and 10 mg/day is the maximum. A 50 mg dose would put the patient at serious risk of severe low blood pressure, reflex tachycardia (a fast heart rate) and shock. Amlodipine has a long half-life, so the effects of an overdose can last a long time.\n\nThis may be a typo for **5 mg** (a common starting dose) or **10 mg**. Could you confirm which dose you meant?\n\n- **5 mg PO once daily**\n- **10 mg PO once daily**\n- Something else. If 50 mg really is intended, please give the clinical reason. I'd still strongly recommend a pharmacist review before it's entered.\n\nOnce you confirm, I'll enter the order."
